  "dhahabi": { "ar": "صدوق", "en": "Truthful.", "source": "al-Kashif 4/523" },
  "bio": "The freed slave of the Companion Salamah ibn al-Akwa', a Madinan Successor whose whole importance lies in one link: he carried Salamah's hadith to the next generation, and because he lived into the 140s his students Abu Asim al-Nabil and al-Makki ibn Ibrahim lived long enough to teach al-Bukhari directly. That is why al-Bukhari's three-link chains from Salamah all pass through him; al-Nawawi notes it in his entry on Salamah. Known by his father's kunya; his own kunya was Abu Khalid.",
